          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "argumentieren — \"to argue (a case), to give arguments\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sie argumentiert gut, aber ich bleibe bei meiner Meinung. She argues well, but I am sticking to my opinion."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It means to reason, not to quarrel; a quarrel is der Streit. Perfekt: hat argumentiert, with no ge-."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "argumentieren is a learned borrowing from Latin argūmentārī \"to bring forward proof, to prove\" (Lewis & Short), from argūmentum \"proof\", with the German verb ending -ieren."
            }
          ]
        },
